                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A supercontinent which formed on Earth approximately 600 million years ago."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20477b99-8ae6-4063-b357-7c123d847d51",
                                                "sense_id": "6ee390b8-fe35-3b16-a0a8-10204d98c60d",
                                                "text": "When Pannotia subsequently split, about 550 million years ago, the interior oceans created by this event, such as lapetus, Tuzo Wilson's so-called 'proto-Atlantic' separating present-day North America from Western Europe, were subsequently destroyed as the next supercontinent (Pangaea) was created."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "987f232b-a701-4ee3-9e59-049628c4ec8b",
                                                "sense_id": "6ee390b8-fe35-3b16-a0a8-10204d98c60d",
                                                "text": "The supercontinent status of Pangaea and Rodinia is undisputed. In contrast, there is ongoing controversy on whether Pannotia existed at all."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
